# Power moves to the other guide in lambda / (2 (n_even - n_odd)) = 31.73 um, from the supermodes of the transverse grid.
# Reference: full transfer at that length, half at half of it. Monitors use the modes of the separate guides, which overlap slightly at small gaps.
title Directional coupler, two 0.5 um guides 250 nm apart
window width=14 length=65.5
guide straight x=-0.375 width=0.5 from=0 to=65.5
guide straight x=0.375 width=0.5 from=0 to=65.5
launch mode x=-0.375 width=0.5
monitor half_cross z=15.75 x=0.375 width=0.5
monitor cross_full z=31.75 x=0.375 width=0.5
monitor bar_full z=31.75 x=-0.375 width=0.5
monitor bar_end z=65.5 x=-0.375 width=0.5
monitor cross_end z=65.5 x=0.375 width=0.5
expect power half_cross 0.494454978 2e-7
expect power cross_full 0.999280960 2e-7
expect power bar_full 0.001285102 2e-7
expect power bar_end 0.989075573 2e-7
expect power cross_end 0.011318392 2e-7
expect neff 2.641330622 2e-8
expect power_above cross_full 0.995
expect power_below bar_full 0.005
expect power half_cross 0.5 0.02
expect sum bar_end cross_end 1.0 0.002
